rules/schrybwys.md and rules/schrybwys-compact.md
-------------------------------------------------
These describe the codified "schriftsprach-nah" spelling system for Bernese
German. That system is not ours. It was established by:

  Werner Marti, "Bärndütschi Schrybwys" (Francke, Bern, 1978) and
  "Berndeutsch-Grammatik" (Francke, Bern, 1985)

  Otto von Greyerz / Ruth Bietenhard, "Berndeutsches Wörterbuch"
  (10th edition, Cosmos, 2017)

and is summarised for the public by berndeutsch.ch, notably in:

  Ursula Pinheiro-Weber, "Bärndütsch schrybe: schriftsprach-nach" (2021),
  licensed CC BY-ND 4.0
  https://www.berndeutsch.ch/doc/berndeutsch-schreiben-schriftsprach-nah-v1.pdf

  Hans Jürg Zingg, "Bärndütsch schrybe: uussprach-nach" (2021), the
  aussprach-nah counterpart, same licence
  https://www.berndeutsch.ch/doc/berndeutsch-schreiben-aussprach-nah-v1.pdf

  https://www.berndeutsch.ch/pages/schrybe (the free summary page)

The rules a spelling system prescribes are facts about that system and are
stated here in our own words and our own arrangement. The illustrative examples
are our own, chosen and verified against berndeutsch.ch dictionary entries with
scripts/bdw, rather than taken from the CC BY-ND documents. Neither CC BY-ND
document is reproduced here in whole or in part, and neither is distributed
with this repository. Read the originals: they are five pages each, they are
free, and they are better than any summary of them.

If Ursula Pinheiro-Weber, Hans Jürg Zingg or berndeutsch.ch consider any part
of rules/ to encroach on their work, open an issue and it will be rewritten or
removed. That is a standing offer, not a formality.

The grammar section
-------------------
The description of Bernese grammar (absence of a preterite, the double perfect,
the frequency of the subjunctive, the declension of zwe/zwo/zwöi and drei/drü,
politeness as the second person plural) follows the Alemannic Wikipedia article
"Berndeutsch", licensed CC BY-SA 4.0:

  https://als.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berndeutsch
  Authors: see the article's history page.

corpus/
-------
corpus/sources.md is ours. corpus/texts/ is not committed to this repository;
it is produced locally by scripts/bd-corpus, which downloads Alemannic
Wikipedia articles licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 and writes the attribution into the
header of every file it creates. If you redistribute those texts, CC BY-SA 4.0
applies to them, not MIT.

berndeutsch.ch
--------------
scripts/bdw queries https://www.berndeutsch.ch, a free Bernese-German
dictionary online since 2000 and run as 100% volunteer work by Stephan Burkard.
The site has no API. bdw therefore behaves like a courteous human reader: one
request per page, a delay between requests, a bounded page walk, a User-Agent
that names this repository, and a link back to every entry instead of a copy of
the dictionary. No dictionary content is stored in this repository.

If you find this useful, the dictionary is the reason. Add the words it is
missing: https://www.berndeutsch.ch/pages/wordaddinfo
